			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Update Cocoon and Mountain submodules\n\nAdvance `Cocoon` to 8c25ad5a to refine code style in the `UriKey` utility by formatting the `fsPath` conditional return statement for improved readability without altering logic.\n\nAdvance `Mountain` to e4c272b2 to introduce `DashboardHelpers` under the `PerformanceDashboard` IPC module. This adds stub utilities for process memory, CPU usage, and UUID generation, alongside a helper to map metric types to display strings, establishing the foundational layer for performance monitoring while maintaining pure function architecture.\n\nThese updates align the extension host and native backend with current coding standards and prepare the IPC layer for future performance metrics integration.",
			"SHA": "e56eef10595c5b6ed53e39aacc7a77a6cfef7b23"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:31:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement Language and Window API handlers and registries\n\nAdvance the `Cocoon` extension host submodule to commit 5aaeeb70. This update introduces foundational logic for VS Code extension API compatibility, specifically bridging language providers and window events with the native Mountain backend.\n\nKey additions include:\n- **Language Provider Handler**: `RegisterProvider` creates auto-assigned handles, notifies Mountain via gRPC (`Context.SendToMountain`), and returns a disposable to unregister providers, handling null inputs gracefully.\n- **URI Normalization**: `UriKey` utility stabilizes map keys from various URI formats to prevent diagnostic collisions.\n- **Window Event Subscription**: `MakeEventSubscriber` wraps `Context.Emitter` to ensure correct `this` binding and standard listener signatures.\n- **Provider Registries**: Centralized `Map` instances for Tree Data, Webview View, and Custom Editor providers enable efficient O(1) lookups by handle, synchronizing state between Cocoon and Mountain.\n\nThese changes enable the extension host to manage VS Code-compliant providers and events, establishing a robust bridge between the extension runtime and the native backend.",
			"SHA": "b1de8927565c8f2b7c32312aa04e34c30dad82a2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:29:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Update Wind submodule with IPC primitives and tracing\n\nAdvance the `Wind` element submodule from commit 32580878 to fd230e54. This update introduces foundational utilities for the UI service layer: `MountainInvoke.ts` encapsulates raw Tauri invocation logic (`InvokeMountain`, `InvokeViaNode`) to centralize native backend communication, while `Trace.ts` provides non-invasive diagnostic tools including `Trace`, `DevLogForward`, and `TimedTrace` for OTEL performance collection and log mirroring to `Mountain.dev.log`.\n\nThese additions remove code duplication from the routing layer and establish a standardized observability surface, enabling structured error handling and performance monitoring across the Wind service architecture.",
			"SHA": "4d997a510e5586420e1092259a3314c158be6178"
		},
